## Results
- Ground-based and satellite measurements have measured a sharp increase in atmospheric CO2 in recent decades. 
- CO2 levels are now 150% the value they were at in 1750 — this is at least 1.5 times greater than the natural increase observed at the end of the last ice age 20,000 years ago



